      <guid isPermaLink="false">fc4f4fd18f6712bc522b674faace38c6a57b6885</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 07 Jul 2026 20:14:30 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4ee407a60a0.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d48f748944.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d48fd7c290.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d49049cfd0.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d49109d805.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d491883858.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d4920ec590.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d492a6e082.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d493847336.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a6b04f81468e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a6b04fe196aa.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d4947e55e4.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a6b04f1d7d46.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d4955df598.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d4962914d7.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d4975f052b.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d496f5b622.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a6b050372dfe.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a4d497df1bdc.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a6b050f07cf9.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a6b05136560b.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a6b051870e29.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;Do you want the true definitive save file to just have fun with, and mess around in, but don't have the courage to do it yourself, don't have the time for it, or have already done it, and don't want to do it again? Well, fret no longer! I went and did it myself, manually, sequentially, the intended way, so you don't have to, if you don't want to, or don't have the time for it! If you wanted a save file like that, then this one here, is the one for you! This save file is actually genuinely 100% complete, with nothing major missing, at all, from across the game in its entirety, and the name is actually Link, so this save can be for absolutely everyone!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For some context, I noticed that the HD Wii U version of this game doesn't have a true 100% save file here on GameBanana, or even across the internet, from what I was able to find, from a lot of thorough researching. There's either always something major missing, or not completed, in some form, or the name isn't Link, in each and every one of the files I would download, and that was very unfortunate to see, as The Wind Waker is my personal favorite Zelda game, so I took it upon myself to truly 100% the game, in essentially all aspects, with no game breaks, or sequence breaks, with the name as Link, playing on Cemu Emulator on PC, for all to enjoy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This mod is fully compatible with Cemu Emulator, which is the recommended way to play the game. This is my follow up mod to the true 100% save file that I posted for the original GameCube version that is here on GameBanana as well! Enjoy it as you please! If you're wondering why Link looks different and more classic, and the buttons on the HUD look more like the original GameCube version in the screenshots I posted, it's because I'm using mods, specifically the GameCube Colored HUD mod by NightSkye and the Beta-styled Link mod by Sven Cakemann, that are both here on GameBanana.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;I completed essentially everything in the game, from start to finish, on 1st quest, with Link's green tunic, as well as 2nd quest, with Link's blue Island Lobster shirt, and the name is Link on both files, so anyone playing can comfortably use this as their own file, and choose which outfit for Link they want to play with, and mess around with, and just have fun. There's even a 3rd file, also named Link, set at Hyrule Castle, before the barrier is broken later in the game, so you can freely use that file to practice and try out the now famous barrier skip glitch.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In this save file, the main story is completed, all sidequests are completed, the Deluxe Pictobox has been collected in the 1st quest, which carries over to the 2nd quest, the Nintendo Gallery is completed in the 1st quest, all figurines are there, which carries over to the 2nd quest too, all items are collected, Magic Armor included, all songs are learned, all heart pieces are collected, all treasure charts are collected, the treasure from said treasure charts are collected, all 60 points have been earned in Beedle's shop membership, and the Silver and Gold membership cards have been collected as a result of such.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Hero's Charm has been collected, the hurricane spin is learned, all the big Octos have been defeated, all Island squares have been mapped out by the Fishman, all of the submarines have been found and completed, all 23 blue Chuchu have been collected, max 99 Joy Pendants have been given to Mrs. Marie, all the upgrades are collected and maxed out, including the wallet that goes up to 5000, bomb bag that goes up to 99, and quiver that goes up to 99, from the various 6 fairy fountains.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;All 4 of the bottles are collected, one is filled with a full bottle of Grandma's Elixir Soup, with the other 3 having half a bottle of Elixir Soup, using the famous soup glitch, or bottle glitch, as you can see in the screenshots I posted, which yes, is possible in the HD Wii U version too, not just the original GameCube version, it's just a lot harder to do, and not as easy, but it is possible, I can confirm this, there's a YouTube video posted by LegendofLuke, that shows the glitch, and I have a comment posted on precisely how to do it, so you can try it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;There are max 5000 rupees, there are 99 arrows and bombs, all dungeons are fully completed, with all the chests in each of them being found and opened, all the hidden Tingle statues are found, both Windfall Island and Link's Oasis are fully decorated, with only the Hero's Flag from the Guru shop on Windfall Island that you receive from completing the trading sequence sidequest, and the potion shop at Windfall Island is completed too. The Hero's Flag is my personal favorite one to decorate with, which is why I used it, but you can change that to your own liking with your own favorite if you want that, of course.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is the absolute definitive save file for the Wii U version of The Legend of&amp;nbsp; Zelda: The Wind Waker HD that you will find online! It took a fairly long while to complete, it was fun to do, beyond enjoyable, and I'm very proud of it! I was glad to do it for others, not just for myself! It was awesome! Have fun with it! May the fortune of the wind be with you!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;u&gt;Installation Instructions:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;br&gt;An extraction tool like Winrar, which is free, is required to extract the file! To apply the save file to Cemu Emulator for use, simply go to File Explorer, on your PC, then your PC drive in "This PC", like the Windows (C:) drive, which also appears as Local Disk (C:), then Users, then your PC's name, then AppData, then Roaming, then Cemu, then mlc01, then usr, then save, then 00050000, then 10143500, then user, then 80000001, then place all 41 files you extracted in there, and it will properly function in the game.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If all this is too confusing, you can also just simply right click on the game in Cemu Emulator on the screen that shows your game list, then go to save directory to get there faster, then user, then 80000001, and that's where those extracted 41 files go. Enjoy!</description>
